Top-down map of a medieval castle exterior and grounds, D&D battle map style, grid squares visible (5ft/square). Mediterranean southern European architecture. Warm parchment tones. Ink and watercolor aesthetic.

REFERENCE: The castle is a cross-shaped building (visible on the Fianus Romanus town map as a black cross) in the southeast of the town, at the border between Aviano and Settebagni quarters. It has its own square curtain wall with round towers at the corners, separate from the town's circular walls.

CASTLE STRUCTURE (center of map):
- MAIN BUILDING: cross-shaped stone keep, two stories, terracotta roof tiles. The cross shape creates four internal courtyards/alcoves between the arms. Arched windows on upper floor. Main entrance (large wooden double doors with iron reinforcements) facing northwest toward town. Above the entrance: the Count's faded coat of arms (illegible, weathered).
- NORTH COURTYARD: enclosed cobblestone yard in the angle of the cross arms. Circular stone WELL (wooden frame, rope, bucket — connects to dungeon L1 below). Single torch on wall. Ivy. Puddles.
- SOUTH WING (arm of the cross): Contessina's quarters. Barred windows.

CASTLE WALLS (square, with corner towers):
- Square curtain wall (3m/10ft high) surrounds the castle grounds. Four ROUND TOWERS at the corners. Crenellated walkway on top (BATTLEMENTS — where balestrieri position in P7). 
- MAIN GATE (northwest face): iron portcullis facing the road into town (Aviano quarter). Two guard posts flanking. Always manned.
- POSTERN GATE (east face): small single door, partially hidden by overgrown bushes. Rarely used. Locked (DC 14).

CASTLE GROUNDS (between walls and keep):
- NORTHWEST APPROACH: road from Aviano arrives here. Open space before the main gate.
- NORTH YARD: the well. Guard patrol route. Practice weapons rack.
- SOUTH SIDE: overgrown garden. Dead fig tree. The postern gate.

MAGAZZINO (STORAGE BUILDING — OUTSIDE castle walls, northeast):
- Separate stone building just outside the northeast section of the castle wall, partially built into the terrain. Heavy wooden door, PADLOCKED from outside (DC 10 to force from inside, DC 14 to pick from outside).
- The staircase from dungeon L1 [A] exits here through a trapdoor in the floor, hidden under old crates.
- INTERIOR: dusty, cobwebbed. Old barrels (empty), farming tools, broken cart wheel, sacks of hardened grain. Trapdoor in back corner under debris.
- EXTERIOR: looks abandoned. Weeds. No windows. Faded sign "Deposito del Castello". Nobody uses it.
- From here, PCs exit directly onto the street in Aviano quarter — no need to enter the castle.

SURROUNDINGS:
- ROAD TO TOWN (northwest): cobblestone road toward Mercato Centrale via Ponte Milvius.
- SETTEBAGNI (southwest): residential quarter, beyond the castle walls.
- AVIANO (north): noble houses along the road (San Giovanni, canonica Don Silverio).

LIGHTING: Daytime. Bright Mediterranean sun.

SCALE: 125x125 meters total (83x83 squares, 1 square = 5ft/1.5m). The castle walls occupy most of the area. The magazzino is outside the walls to the northeast.

COLOR PALETTE: Warm sandstone beige for walls, terracotta orange for roofs, dusty green for vegetation, grey cobblestone, dark brown for wood. Castle in darker stone than surrounding buildings.

LABELS: elegant italic font. "Castello del Conte", "Cortile Nord", "Pozzo", "Magazzino", "Porta Principale", "Spalti", "Postierla", "Strada per Fianus".
